Write a starter treerig.toml at the root of the Git repository you run it in,
naming the Compose file found there (compose.yaml if none), with a commented-out
service and hooks to fill in. It refuses to replace an existing treerig.toml.
Run `treerig config validate` afterwards. It reads no treerig.toml, so --config
is refused.

Usage:
  treerig init [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for init

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
